# Base URL of the LifeLink backend, including the /api/v1 prefix.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the JS bundle at build time, so this is the only
# supported way to point the app at a backend. Leave it unset and the app derives the host from
# the Expo dev server (see src/config/env.ts) — that is usually correct for `expo start`.
#
# Set it explicitly when the derived host is wrong, or when pointing at a non-local backend:
#
#   LAN device / Expo Go on a phone   http://192.168.1.42:3000/api/v1   <- your machine's LAN IP
#   Android emulator (AVD)            http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/v1
#   Genymotion                        http://10.0.3.2:3000/api/v1
#   iOS simulator                     http://localhost:3000/api/v1
#
# `localhost` on a physical device means the phone itself and will never reach your backend.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
